      "text": "Model a trapped particle of mass $m$ with the **infinite square well**: potential energy $V(x) = 0$ inside a box of width $L$ ($0 < x < L$) and $V(x) = \\infty$ outside.\n\nBecause an infinite barrier is impenetrable, the wavefunction vanishes outside: $\\psi(x) = 0$. A physical wavefunction must be continuous, so $\\psi$ is pinned to zero at both walls:\n\n$$\\psi(0) = 0 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\psi(L) = 0$$\n\nThese **boundary conditions** act just like the two fixed ends of a plucked guitar string.",
